<section class="sub-hero"><div class="sub-hero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roof-shingles.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roof-shingles-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roof-shingles.webp 960w" sizes="100vw" width="960" height="640" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.1"></div><div class="shell sub-hero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span><a href="/utah-appraisal-services/">Services</a><span class="sep">›</span><span aria-current="page">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</span></nav><p class="kicker">Appraisal service</p><h1>Roof and Hail Damage Appraisal for Utah Properties</h1><p class="lede">Summer storms along the Wasatch Front and in Cache and Utah valleys can drop hail fast and leave damage that’s easy to miss from the ground. We document roofs slope by slope and price them completely.</p><div class="row-btns"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/contact-utah-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>Season</dt><dd>Mostly May–September</dd></div><div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Measurements &amp; scope</dd></div><div><dt>Roof types</dt><dd>Asphalt, metal, tile, flat</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="shell two-col"><article class="prose">
<h2>Common reasons roof claims are underpaid</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Partial approvals.</strong> A carrier approves the south and west slopes but leaves the north and east, even when the shingles can’t be matched or the damage pattern is the same.</li>
<li><strong>Measurement errors.</strong> Squares calculated from a footprint without the right pitch factor, or waste set too low for a cut-up roof.</li>
<li><strong>Missing items.</strong> Starter, ridge cap, drip edge, ice-and-water shield, step flashing, vents, satellite detach and reset, and steep or high-roof charges.</li>
<li><strong>Cosmetic arguments.</strong> Disagreements over whether dents to metal roofing or vents are functional damage, which depend heavily on policy wording.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How we document a roof</h2>
<p>We measure each plane, record pitch, and photograph hail hits in test squares on every slope. Soft metals such as vents, gutters and downspouts tell part of the story; so do window screens, siding and fences. We pair that field record with weather data for your address and the date of loss.</p>
<h2>Utah-specific roof issues</h2>
<p>Many Utah codes call for ice barrier underlayment along eaves where ice dams are common, and mountain homes often carry snow guards, heat cable and heavier sheathing. Estimates written without those details tend to come up short. Utah County and Salt Lake County subdivisions also have plenty of steep, cut-up roofs where waste and labor factors matter.</p>
<h2>Try the numbers first</h2>
<p>Our free <a href="/utah-claim-calculators/roof-pitch-squares-estimator/">roof pitch and squares estimator</a> shows how pitch and waste change the total. It’s a useful check before you talk to anyone.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How soon after a hailstorm should I file?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>As soon as you reasonably can. Policies require prompt notice, and the longer you wait the harder it is to tie damage to a specific storm.</p></div></details><details><summary>The adjuster said the damage is cosmetic. Can appraisal help?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>Possibly. Whether damage is functional is often a factual question appraisers address, but some policies have specific cosmetic-damage exclusions that are coverage issues. We’ll read the policy with you.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can appraisal require a full roof replacement?<span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="ans"><p>The panel values what it takes to repair the covered damage. If repair can’t be done properly without replacing more, the award can reflect that, depending on the policy and the evidence.</p></div></details></div><h2>Related services</h2><div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel" href="/utah-appraisal-services/canyon-wind-damage-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Wind &amp; Tornado Damage Appraisal</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/utah-appraisal-services/snow-ice-freeze-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Snow Load, Ice Dam &amp; Freeze Appraisal</span><svg class="ico sm" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel" href="/utah-appraisal-services/water-pipe-leak-appraisal/"><small>Service</small><span>Water &amp; Leak Damage Appraisal</